| Person | Commits in window | Lines still in code today |
|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | `02afce3` test: vary header coverage (2026-04-10)<br>`b2005d9` lib: annotate handlers (2026-04-10) | 261 total across all their history, 37 of them from these two commits (36 from `02afce3`, 1 from `b2005d9`) |
| Vansh Sharma | `5317ebe` docs: app.del() with app.delete() in README example (#411) (2026-04-07) | 1 (the README line) |

- **Troy Goode** committed from two email addresses (`<email redacted>` and `troy@laptop.example`). I counted them once, combining both in the 261.
- **Fiona Formatter** (`62628c0`, 2026-04-12) is excluded as a formatting-only commit. Its subject is "reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes", and it changes 291 lines across four files. Note that `git show -w` does not make it empty, because quote changes are not whitespace. Its reformatting is also why `b2005d9`'s 12 changed lines show only 1 surviving line. Fiona's reformat accounts for 1016 lines in the current code, the largest single share, but I left it out as you asked.
- **Bots:** none committed in the window. The dependabot commits are older.

The line counts come from `git blame HEAD` over the 18 tracked files, attributed by author name.

